 "definitions": "Measurement of rule_step2.md: bright-only second Newton step of the 1M pair.\n\nusage: [PERGAL=_faintdraw] python step2.py [run dir]   (default debug/step2; PERGAL picks pergal_<side><PERGAL>.npz\n  (rule_faintdraw.md: faint galaxies from the drawn-start rerun; the it0 reproduction check is then skipped); light: reads pergal_<side>.npz (it0) and <run dir>/comoving;\n  refuses until all units of truth_units.txt are done. Another run dir, e.g. debug/truth, is a code test only and\n  writes step2_result_<dir>.json)\nit0: s_i(0) = raw score - dlogZ/dg (pooled selection chunks of both sides), I = sum (s s^T - E), as pair_step.py\n(reproduced first as a check). Bright (mag < 21, the galaxies of truth_units.txt): t_i = s_i(g1) + I_i g1 with\ns_i(g1) from the comoving_circ ratios at the sampled shear g1 and the same selection term; others t_i = s_i(0).\ng2 = I^-1 sum t. Errors as pair_step.estimate (scene units; chain part from chain halves; selection from the chunk\nscatter; bootstrap over scenes). The truth is read only in the last block, after step2_result.json is written.\n",
